  "confidence": "high",
  "answer": "When you delete a widget's key from `st.session_state`, the widget does not revert to its default value immediately. Instead, the frontend retains the old value until the next rerun, at which point it will adopt the stale value from the frontend. This behavior is due to how Streamlit handles widget identity and state, specifically that deleting a key does not reset the widget to its default value during the current run.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "1",
      "text": "If the widget has a key that was deleted from `st.session_state`, then Streamlit will recreate the key using the current frontend value.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "2",
      "text": "Deleting a key from Session State will not revert the widget to a default value.",
      "citation_ids": ["S1"]
