  "answer": "The behavior you're experiencing is expected due to how Streamlit handles widget state in multipage apps. Each widget's identity is tied to the page it is created on, so when you switch pages, the widget resets to its default value. To maintain state across pages, you can use a separate key in `st.session_state` to save the widget's value independently from the widget itself, as described in the documentation.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "1",
      "text": "If you define an identical widget on two different pages, then the widget will reset to its default value when you switch pages.",
